      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree with this plan.  This driver really belongs under the `zephyr/` directory.  The `zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq` subsystem is currently tightly coupled to the x86 architecture, so I think more analysis is needed as to whether qcom support can be added to `ap_pwrseq`.  Another possible path is port `qcom_exp` to `zephyr/drivers/pmic/pmic_qcom_exp.c` as a standalone Zephyr driver.\nPlease open a bug to track this.",
